        "original_id": "f93043d5-d3f3-5fe4-9202-b2990cb90597",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Woggle-Bug, The Marvelous Land of Oz, The Wonderful Wizard of Oz\n- People: L. Frank Baum, Frederic Chapin, Frank Smithson\n- Organizations: Shubert Organization\n- Places: Garrick Theater, Chicago\n\nFacts:\n- The Wonderful Wizard of Oz was published in 1900.\n- The Marvelous Land of Oz was published on July 5, 1904.\n- The Marvelous Land of Oz was written by L. Frank Baum.\n- The Marvelous Land of Oz is the second of L. Frank Baum's Oz books and a sequel to The Wonderful Wizard of Oz.\n- The Woggle-Bug is a musical based on The Marvelous Land of Oz.\n- The Woggle-Bug has a book and lyrics by L. Frank Baum and music by Frederic Chapin.\n- The Woggle-Bug opened on June 18, 1905, at the Garrick Theater in Chicago.\n- The Woggle-Bug was directed by Frank Smithson, a Shubert Organization employee.",
